{
  "dom_id": "step-q107001",
  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the matrix $C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(C-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )(-18-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +18) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-18$ and $\\lambda =6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal.",
